{
  "id": "dative-verbs",
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "Dativverben",
  "group": "Cases",
  "sourceFile": "dativverben.html",
  "overview": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Some verbs assign dative to their person or thing even when English does not use “to.” Learn each verb together with + dative."
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "",
        "rows": [
          [
            "Verb",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          [
            "helfen",
            "help",
            "Ich helfe dir."
          ],
          [
            "danken",
            "thank",
            "Wir danken Ihnen."
          ],
          [
            "gefallen",
            "be pleasing to",
            "Das gefällt mir."
          ],
          [
            "gehören",
            "belong to",
            "Das Buch gehört ihm."
          ],
          [
            "antworten",
            "answer",
            "Sie antwortet dem Lehrer."
          ],
          [
            "folgen",
            "follow",
            "Der Hund folgt der Frau."
          ],
          [
            "glauben",
            "believe",
            "Ich glaube dir."
          ],
          [
            "passen",
            "fit/suit",
            "Die Schuhe passen mir."
          ],
          [
            "schmecken",
            "taste good to",
            "Die Suppe schmeckt uns."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Verbs of giving or communicating often use a dative person plus an accusative thing: jemandem etwas erzählen, sagen, schreiben, schenken, or zeigen."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Gefallen reverses the English viewpoint: Das Lied gefällt mir literally means “The song is pleasing to me.” The liked thing is nominative; the person is dative."
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "content": "",
        "de": "Kannst du mir helfen?",
        "note": "mir is dative after helfen"
      }
    ]
  },
